segments.en:
His merit he left behind him — for all who walk in his ways,
    for each one according to his deeds — as one draws down upon oneself his rectifications:
    — He is our Rabbainu.

A novelty such as he has never existed — from the beginning of the world until the end of the world;
    from many worlds his name is hidden — yet he will rectify the world, for this is the entirety of man:
    — He is our Rabbainu.

Despair does not exist in the world at all — those who draw close to him will ascend from the pit of destruction,
    if they cast aside their imagined wisdoms and do as he commands them in wholeness:
    — He is our Rabbainu.

Our soul has yearned for its root — but our adversary has grown very mighty;
    we have almost perished in our vanities — were it not for the help of our Rabbainu:
    — He is our Rabbainu.
